From 7214075cb97d0dbe55746012c680e1f2f8cb8e74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zack Maril <zmaril@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:46:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add `-Zheadstart`: start units on dependencies' early
 metadata

With `-Zheadstart`, Cargo passes `-Zearly-metadata` to rustc, which then
writes early metadata (`.early-rmeta`) once a crate's item interfaces are
checked, before its function bodies are, and announces it with an
`early-metadata` artifact notification. Cargo starts the crate's
dependents on that notification:

- Every unit compiled by rustc, in check, build or test mode, starts on
  its rlib dependencies' early metadata: libraries, binaries, tests,
  proc macros and build scripts. Proc-macro and dylib dependencies are
  still built first. This extends pipelining, which started `cargo build`
  libraries on the full metadata, to every unit, and to `cargo check`.
- A unit's dependents are released on whichever metadata comes first.
- A unit that links no longer waits for the full build of every
  transitive dependency: rustc waits for the rlibs itself, before
  linking.

Freshness still treats a unit that links as depending on its
dependencies' rlibs, not only their metadata: starting it on metadata
doesn't change what its output is built from.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
