+## headstart
+* Tracking Issue: None yet
+
+The `-Z headstart` flag starts compiling a crate as soon as its dependencies'
+item interfaces are checked, instead of waiting for their function bodies to be
+checked too. It needs a nightly rustc with `-Zearly-metadata`, which Cargo
+passes to every compilation:
+
+* rustc writes *early metadata* (`.early-rmeta`) once a crate's interfaces are
+  checked, and announces it with an `early-metadata` artifact notification.
+  Cargo starts the crate's dependents then, for `cargo check`, `cargo build`
+  and `cargo test`, including binaries, tests, proc macros and build scripts.
+* A dependent does all its analysis against early metadata. Before code
+  generation, rustc swaps in the dependency's full metadata, and before linking
+  it waits for the dependency's rlib.
+
+```toml
+[unstable]
+headstart = true
+```
+
 ## builtin-dependencies
 * Tracking Issue: [rust-lang/cargo#16960](https://github.com/rust-lang/cargo/issues/16960)
 - RFC: [rust-lang/rfcs#3875](https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/3875-build-std-explicit-dependencies.html)
diff --git a/src/compiler/build_runner/mod.rs b/src/compiler/build_runner/mod.rs
index 4bf69f6..2f74bbe 100644
--- a/src/compiler/build_runner/mod.rs
+++ b/src/compiler/build_runner/mod.rs
@@ -763,6 +763,22 @@ impl<'a, 'gctx> BuildRunner<'a, 'gctx> {
     /// Returns whether when `parent` depends on `dep` if it only requires the
     /// metadata file from `dep`.
     pub fn only_requires_rmeta(&self, parent: &Unit, dep: &Unit) -> bool {
+        // Headstart: a compile unit starts on its library dependencies' early
+        // metadata (`-Zearly-metadata`), written before their bodies are
+        // checked. Check units need nothing more. Units that generate code
+        // wait for full metadata before code generation, and units that link
+        // wait for the rlibs before linking; rustc does both. Dependencies
+        // that must be fully built (proc macros, dylibs) still are.
+        if self.headstart_enabled() && headstart_starts_early(parent, dep) {
+            return true;
+        }
+        self.only_requires_rmeta_file(parent, dep)
+    }
+
+    /// Returns whether `parent`'s output depends only on `dep`'s metadata
+    /// file, so that only its mtime matters for freshness. Headstart starts
+    /// more units on metadata, but a unit that links still uses the rlib.
+    pub fn only_requires_rmeta_file(&self, parent: &Unit, dep: &Unit) -> bool {
         // We're only a candidate for requiring an `rmeta` file if we
         // ourselves are building an rlib,
         !parent.requires_upstream_objects()
@@ -773,6 +789,13 @@ impl<'a, 'gctx> BuildRunner<'a, 'gctx> {
             && dep.mode == CompileMode::Build
     }
 
+    /// Whether headstart is on (`-Zheadstart`): units are compiled with
+    /// `-Zearly-metadata`, and a unit's dependents start as soon as its early
+    /// metadata is written, before its function bodies are checked.
+    pub fn headstart_enabled(&self) -> bool {
+        self.bcx.gctx.cli_unstable().headstart
+    }
+
     /// Returns whether when `unit` is built whether it should emit metadata as
     /// well because some compilations rely on that.
     pub fn rmeta_required(&self, unit: &Unit) -> bool {
@@ -816,3 +839,19 @@ impl<'a, 'gctx> BuildRunner<'a, 'gctx> {
         }
     }
 }
+
+/// Whether, with headstart, `parent` can start on `dep`'s early metadata.
+fn headstart_starts_early(parent: &Unit, dep: &Unit) -> bool {
+    let compiled_by_rustc = matches!(
+        parent.mode,
+        CompileMode::Build | CompileMode::Test | CompileMode::Check { .. }
+    );
+    let dep_is_rlib = dep.target.is_lib() && !dep.requires_upstream_objects();
+    compiled_by_rustc
+        && dep_is_rlib
+        && if parent.mode.is_check() {
+            dep.mode == (CompileMode::Check { test: false })
+        } else {
+            dep.mode == CompileMode::Build
+        }
+}
